  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-40185",
      "knowledge_point_id": "cbff5997-1801-5dec-8e3d-e3d1ff309015",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Using a Given Graph",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/62502a59f15828ddfe1850039930128c0c382b072504725038ecaac9b9b90196.png)\n\nGiven the sketch of a polynomial $p(x)$ above, find the solution to $p(x)<0.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve the inequality $p(x)<0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=p(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (-2,1)\\cup (1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/9b283fb0afe6a6f8bf6950765bbcb845c1262b01c278cc7bdca20b6fe14280ff.png)",
