  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-87672",
      "knowledge_point_id": "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Containing No Constant Term",
      "problem": "Given $P(x)=12{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{4},$ solve $P(x)>0.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & =12{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{4} \\\\  & =-({x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-x-12) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+3x-12) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}(x(x-4)+3(x-4)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}(x+3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=12{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}$ are $x=-3,$ $x=0$ and $x=4,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-3$ and $x=4$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/5ebfbd4e18de00fad05c4192be2147a9b9765e00fae5b74ac608e85466c21e73.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is \n\n$$\nx\\in (-3,0)\\cup (0,4).\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in (-4,\\infty )",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in (-3,4)",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in (-3,0)\\cup (0,4)",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (3,\\infty )",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in (-4,0)\\cup (0,3)",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
